// Coordination with conflicting preferences ("Battle of the Sexes").
// Both players want to choose the same venue; Alice prefers the opera, Bob the fight.
// The choices are simultaneous, so the compiler commits both before either opens.
//
// Either common choice is an equilibrium. Moving first would let a player pick its
// favourite and force the other to follow, so disclosing a choice early is a
// profitable deviation that the source game does not allow: this is what the
// terminal audit deters (see docs/AUDITED-RUNTIME.md).
//
// Payoffs (pot = 20): meet at the favourite venue 16 / 4; miss each other 1 / 1, burn 18.

game main() {
  join Alice() $ 10 Bob() $ 10;
  yield or split Alice(opera: bool) Bob(opera: bool);
  withdraw (Alice.opera && Bob.opera) ? { Alice -> 16; Bob -> 4 }
         : (!Alice.opera && !Bob.opera) ? { Alice -> 4; Bob -> 16 }
         : { Alice -> 1; Bob -> 1; burn 18 }
}
